  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "The art club was holding a Saturday workshop.",
      "Nina made a notice with the date, time, room number and a list of materials.",
      "She checked every detail and felt that the notice was complete."
    ],
    [
      "However, only two students signed up during the first week.",
      "Nina asked several classmates whether they had seen it.",
      "Most had not: the notice was behind an open door, where it was not clearly visible."
    ],
    [
      "She changed its position to a board beside the main entrance.",
      "She kept the date, time and room number exactly the same.",
      "A large heading helped people understand the subject before reading the details."
    ],
    [
      "More students noticed the workshop the next day.",
      "The small change in position had made a significant difference.",
      "Nina still checked that new readers understood where to go.",
      "Completing a notice was one task; making sure people could find and use the information was another."
    ]
  ],
  "translations": [
    "美术社要在星期六举办一次工作坊。",
    "妮娜做了一张通知，写上日期、时间、教室编号和材料清单。",
    "她检查了每个细节，觉得通知已经完整了。",
    "然而，第一周只有两位学生报名。",
    "妮娜问了几位同学是否看见过通知。",
    "大多数人没有看见：通知贴在一扇打开的门后，不够显眼。",
    "她把通知的位置换到了主入口旁的布告栏。",
    "日期、时间和教室编号都保持原样。",
    "一个大标题帮助大家先了解主题，再阅读细节。",
    "第二天，更多学生注意到了这个工作坊。",
    "位置上的小变化带来了明显的不同。",
    "妮娜仍然检查，新读到通知的人是否知道该去哪里。",
    "完成一张通知是一项任务；确保大家能找到并使用信息，是另一项任务。"
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": "Why had most classmates missed the first notice?",
      "options": [
        "It did not include a date or room number.",
        "Its position made it difficult to see.",
        "The club had not planned a workshop."
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "evidence": [
        1,
        2,
        5
      ],
      "explanation": "通知内容完整，但位置不显眼。不能把“没人注意到”误解成“信息没写全”。"
    },
    {
      "prompt": "What is the main idea of the last sentence?",
      "options": [
        "A complete notice is useful only if people can find and understand it.",
        "Writing any details on a notice is unnecessary.",
        "Moving a notice always guarantees that everyone will join."
      ],
      "correct": 0,
      "evidence": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "explanation": "结尾区分“写完”与“让信息发挥作用”。文中没有保证每个人都会报名。"
    }
  ],
  "sentenceHelp": [
    {
      "pattern": "visible / invisible",
      "help": "visible 表示“看得见的、显眼的”；invisible 表示“看不见的”。本文 not clearly visible 表示不够显眼，并非物体不存在。"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "complete / completing",
      "help": "complete 可作形容词“完整的”，也可作动词“完成”；Completing 在末句中指“完成通知这件事”。"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "significant difference",
      "help": "significant 在这里表示差别“明显、重要”，没有在进行统计显著性检验。要按语境选词义。"
    }
  ],
